Prospectus Summary
Overview
AI is Transforming Intelligence
We believe that Powerful AI, a highly capable and impactful form of frontier AI characterized by the following key attributes, will become widely available within a few years:
• cognitive capabilities matching or exceeding those of top human experts across most professional and scientific disciplines;
• the ability to navigate all interfaces available to a human working virtually, including text, audio, video, and direct computer control;
• the ability to reason through complex tasks autonomously over extended periods—lasting hours, days, or weeks—and seek clarification and feedback when needed;
• the ability to coordinate across multiple instances and collaborate with both humans and other AI systems; and

The Offering
The number of shares of our Class A common stock, Class N common stock, Class T common stock, and Class F common stock that will be outstanding after this offering is based on shares of our Class A common stock, shares of our Class N common stock, one share of our Class T common stock, and one share of our Class F common stock outstanding as of September 30, 2026, which reflects:
• the automatic conversion of (i) all outstanding shares of our Series A, C-1, D-1, D-2, E-1, F-1, G-1, and H-1 redeemable convertible preferred stock into shares of Class A common stock and (ii) all outstanding shares of our Series B, C-2, D-3, E-2, E-3, E-4, E-5, F-2, G-2, G-3, G-4, H-2, H-3, and H-4 redeemable convertible preferred stock into shares of Class N common stock, immediately prior to the completion of this offering pursuant to the terms of our amended and restated certificate of incorporation (collectively, the “Preferred Stock Conversion”);

The Offering
• one share of our Class F common stock that will be issued immediately prior to the completion of this offering to the Founder LLC (the “Class F Stock Issuance”);
• the conversion of $ in aggregate principal amount of our outstanding convertible promissory notes into shares of Class N common stock immediately prior to the completion of this offering, representing shares issuable to Amazon Web Services, Inc. upon the completion of this offering without causing it to exceed the applicable ownership cap (the “Convertible Notes Conversion”);
• the Initial Public Benefit Issuance, the shares of which (i) are considered legally outstanding, (ii) are not considered outstanding for accounting purposes while held by our wholly owned subsidiary, and (iii) accordingly will not be reflected as outstanding in our consolidated financial statements; and

The Offering
• shares of our Class A common stock issuable upon the exercise of options to purchase shares of our Class A common stock outstanding as of September 30, 2026, with a weighted-average exercise price of $ per share;
• shares of our Class A common stock issuable upon the vesting and settlement of RSUs outstanding as of the date of this prospectus, but for which (i) the service-based vesting condition was not satisfied as of such date and (ii) the performance-based vesting condition, if applicable, will be satisfied upon the effectiveness of the registration statement of which this prospectus forms a part;
• shares of our Class A common stock issued after September 30, 2026 in connection with our acquisitions of privately-held companies; and
• shares of our Class A common stock reserved for future issuance under our equity compensation plans, consisting of:

The Offering
◦ shares of our Class A common stock reserved for future issuance upon conversion of Class N common stock issuable under our Donation Matching Plan (as amended and restated, the “Donation Matching Plan”);
◦ shares of our Class A common stock to be reserved for future issuance under our 2026 Equity Incentive Plan (our “2026 Plan”), which will become effective prior to the completion of this offering;
◦ shares of our Class A common stock reserved for future issuance under our Amended and Restated 2021 Stock Plan (our “2021 Plan”) as of September 30, 2026, which number of shares will be added to the shares of our Class A common stock to be reserved for future issuance under our 2026 Plan upon its effectiveness, at which time we will cease granting awards under our 2021 Plan; and
◦ shares of our Class A common stock to be reserved for future issuance under our 2026 Employee Stock Purchase Plan (our “ESPP”), which will become effective prior to the completion of this offering.

The Offering
Our 2026 Plan and ESPP each provide for an annual automatic increase in the number of shares of our Class A common stock reserved thereunder, and our 2026 Plan provides for increases to the number of shares that may be granted thereunder based on awards under our 2021 Plan that expire or are cancelled or forfeited, and shares under our 2021 Plan that are tendered to or withheld by us for payment of an exercise price or for satisfying tax withholding obligations or are forfeited or otherwise repurchased by us, as more fully described in the section titled “Executive Compensation—Equity Plans.”
Except as otherwise indicated, all information in this prospectus assumes:
• the Preferred Stock Conversion will occur immediately prior to the completion of this offering;
• the Convertible Notes Conversion will occur immediately prior to the completion of this offering;

The Offering
